The function handles potential memory allocation failures gracefully and manages all dynamically allocated memory to prevent leaks. It integrates an external data source for generating the random strings and offsets, considering the delays and variable response times it may introduce. Efficiently allocates and deallocates memory to optimize performance, especially when dealing with larger datasets. The code includes comments explaining design choices and trade-offs.

To safely free all allocated memory and avoid leaks, the `free_arrays` function is provided. This function iterates through the arrays and frees each dynamically allocated buffer before freeing the main array pointers.']

