5. Implement error handling to manage invalid inputs and unexpected null pointers gracefully.
6. Consider the integration of this data structure with an external data source, which may impose specific constraints on memory usage and update frequency.
7. Design the code to be modular and easily extensible for future enhancements.

Return only the code for this function, assuming the following structure for `struct node`:

